/-- **Proposition 6.1** (lines 919-936) in the form used in Section 7: for every smooth compactly
supported spatial cutoff `χ` there are `C, σ > 0` such that, for smooth cutoffs `ψ` supported in
`[A,B]`, `L ≥ 1` and bounded measurable `u_1, u_2`,
`‖χ T_ψ(f_1, f_2)‖_1 ≤ C ‖ψ‖_{C^20} L^{-σ} ‖u_1‖_∞ ‖u_2‖_∞` for the two input configurations
`(f_1, f_2) = (ψ(D_1/L) u_1, φ(D_2/L) u_2)` and `(φ(2D_1/L) u_1, ψ(D_2/L) u_2)` (one annular and one
bounded frequency input). -/
